   "en": "Cheonjae, sesang-eul ilgda"
  },
  "altTitles": [
   {
    "en": "The Genius Who Sees Through the World"
   },
   {
    "en": "The Genius Who Reads the World"
   },
   {
    "ko": "천재, 세상을 읽다"
   },
   {
    "en": "Genius, Read the Worlds"
   }
  ],
  "description": {
   "en": "As a child, Shin Woo-jin was kidnapped and locked away in a warehouse, forced to live as a slave.\n\nBut against all odds, he was rescued and finally stepped into the outside world.\n\nThough free, Woo-jin wasn’t like other children.\n\nHe had an extraordinary gift—the ability to read people.\nBy observing the smallest facial expressions and unconscious gestures, he could see through their thoughts, emotions, and intentions with near-perfect accuracy.\n\nLike a profiler, like a modern-day Sherlock, Woo-jin learned to navigate the world, one observation at a time.\n\nBut for someone who sees too much, living an ordinary life is the hardest thing of all.\n\nAll he ever wanted was a peaceful, simple life.\n\nBut the world had other plans.\n\n“As I thought… living a normal life is far too difficult.”"
  },
